Make migrations hand-runnable: fix a cross-migration dependency, add an all-in-one file

Migration 000009 declared a foreign key inline to public.admin_uploads, a table
created by 000006. On a database where 000006 had not been applied -- which is
what happened -- it failed with "relation public.admin_uploads does not exist",
an error that gives no hint about the real cause.

- The foreign key is now added in a guarded DO block that only runs when
  admin_uploads exists, so 000009 no longer depends on being run after 000006.
- New supabase/ALL_MIGRATIONS.sql: every migration concatenated in filename
  order, generated by scripts/build-all-migrations.mjs (npm run build:migrations).
  Every statement is idempotent, so it can be run in one paste and re-run safely.
  This removes the ordering hazard entirely for a by-hand workflow.
- Verified all CREATE TABLE statements across all migrations use IF NOT EXISTS.

Note this also explains why vision was non-functional: describe_asset reads
admin_uploads to locate the file, and that table did not exist.
